            "old_string": "### 51.4 Span-level judgment cache\n- [ ] Cache LLM disambiguation results so repeated encounters of the\n      same term in similar contexts skip the LLM entirely.\n  - Cache key (judgment ABI, 10 fields):\n    `{ ruleset_hash: blake3, judgment_prompt_version: u32,\n    local_disambig_version: u32, cost_mode, profile, content_type,\n    normalized_context, ambiguous_term, candidate_set_hash: blake3,\n    model_family }`.  Use blake3 (already a dependency) consistently\n    -- no SHA-256 algorithm proliferation.  `ruleset_hash` covers\n    both embedded ruleset and external OpenCC dependency changes --\n    silent modifications to OpenCC TWPhrases/TWVariants bypass simple\n    version integers.  Precompute `ruleset_hash` in `build.rs`\n    (extends 49.2) rather than re-hashing at every process start.\n    A ruleset change must yield 0 hits on prior entries.\n    (Gemini+Codex review: `rule_version` alone is too weak.)\n  - Value: `{ chosen_replacement, confidence, explanation_text,\n    timestamp, model_family }`.  Store full rationale text (not just\n    hash) so cached hits can still surface reasoning in `explain` or\n    `max_accuracy` mode.  Compress with zstd if entry exceeds 200\n    bytes.  (Gemini review round 2: hash-only prevents displaying\n    rationale on cache hits, conflicting with 51.6 transparency.)\n  - Storage: `~/.config/zhtw-mcp/judgment_cache.json` (same pattern\n    as override/suppression stores).  Schema-versioned with\n    backup-and-reset on mismatch.\n  - Context normalization: strip whitespace runs, lowercase ASCII,\n    truncate to ±40 chars, include candidate-set digest and\n    normalization-version field.  Add negative tests proving two\n    distinct contexts that normalize similarly do not alias.\n    (Codex review: ±30 chars too narrow for 30-day persistence.)\n  - TTL: bounded unsigned duration, clamped to max 365 days.  `0`\n    means disabled.  Store `expires_at` using checked `SystemTime`\n    arithmetic.  Default 30 days.  `zhtw-mcp cache clear` subcommand.\n    (Codex review: unbounded day count risks overflow.)\n  - Scope: new `src/rules/judgment_cache.rs`, wired into\n    `src/mcp/sampling.rs`.\n  - Gate: (a) second scan of same document with same ambiguous terms\n    produces zero LLM calls, hit rate ≥80%.  (b) `ruleset_hash`\n    bump invalidates all entries.  (c) prompt/schema version bump\n    invalidates.  (d) expired entries evicted.  (e) two similar\n    contexts that differ semantically do not share a cached judgment.",
